# FerrosaDB on __CLUSTER_NAME__

Workload: FerrosaDB, one pod on each db node (__DB_NODE_COUNT__ db nodes)
Region: __REGION__
DB node private IPs: __DB_NODE_IPS__

## Quick start

```bash
easy-db-lab ferrosa start                    # ghcr.io/ferrosadb/ferrosa:nightly, data on the node's disk
easy-db-lab ferrosa start --version=<tag>    # another tag of ghcr.io/ferrosadb/ferrosa
easy-db-lab ferrosa start --image=<ref>      # a full image reference, e.g. a custom build in your ECR
easy-db-lab ferrosa stop                     # remove the pods; the data and the claims stay
easy-db-lab kit info ferrosa                 # every start option and endpoint
```

Only 3 or more db nodes is the tested topology.

## Endpoints

Every endpoint answers on the private IP of every db node and reaches the first pod (`ferrosa-0`). Authentication is off.

| Endpoint | NodePort | Connect with |
|---|---|---|
| CQL | 30942 | `cqlsh <db-node-ip> 30942` |
| Console, `/metrics`, `/readyz` | 30909 | `http://<db-node-ip>:30909/` |
| Bolt | 30787 | `bolt://<db-node-ip>:30787` |
| Graph HTTP API | 30747 | `http://<db-node-ip>:30747` |
| SPARQL | 30880 | `http://<db-node-ip>:30880` |
| Postgres wire stub | 30532 | `psql -h <db-node-ip> -p 30532` |
| Arrow Flight | 30815 | `grpc://<db-node-ip>:30815` |

Inside the cluster, pod `i` is also `ferrosa-<i>.default.svc.cluster.local` (CQL 9042).

## Data

Each pod keeps its data in `/var/lib/ferrosa`, the platform PV on its db node's data disk (`/mnt/db1/ferrosa`). With `--storage=s3` FerrosaDB keeps its data in the cluster data bucket under `ferrosa/`. `--heap-profile` writes `.heap` files to `/var/lib/ferrosa/heap-profiles/`.
